    "created_at": "2015-11-11T12:05:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-11T12:05:11Z",
    "body": "The best I can think of is that rather than a copy we create a list of pointers. And then when a listener is removed some kind of \"removed flag\" gets set that is checked by the invoke algorithm. The concept of iteration over a live list isn't really defined (ideally IDL would define some constructs for us).\n\nWould that work @bzbarsky?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
